WEBVTT

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.580
You think an apology will suffice?

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:24.600
We lost a valuable fighter.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.520
Tsubaki, surely you understand now.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.090
We can't work with these sinners.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:34.050
Your naivete brought about this outcome.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.270
They are our enemies.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.470
You're wrong. We're not your enemies.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.410
Ridiculous.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:44.470
You were just betrayed by 
a woman you believed your ally.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:45.720
Yuri is...

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.730
I don't wish to be stabbed in the back.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.050
Never contact us again.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.870
Tsubaki-chan.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:56.240
Here.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.250
We don't need your pebbles.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.180
Pebbles? These are—

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.540
What is it, then?

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:09.360
Kurokami Marie is gone.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.340
You think returning that to us
 will make us forgive you?

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.180
I don't have time for this.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.260
Tsubaki-chan...

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:01.030
<b>Sometimes People Become
 Cheerful When Faced With Death</b>

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:07.610
Fog density stable at over 98%.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:11.640
Hey. Show your face already.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.640
You must be bored to death
 "conserving your strength."

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:14.920
Begin the test.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.920
Artificial keystone 6, final test.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.130
Resonance volume at maximum strength.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.100
Excellent.

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:47.990
A shame things didn't go as planned.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.430
Befriending an agent of Chaos
 was the pinnacle of foolishness.

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:53.800
"We can change fate"?

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.610
Is this the result of that?

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:58.880
Our relationship with the
 Guardian State is ruined.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:00.590
What will you do now?

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:02.760
I don't know.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:07.040
Kurokami died because she trusted you!

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.790
And you "don't know"?!

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:13.810
How many people do you have to kill
 before you're satisfied, grim reaper?

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.830
I'm sorry, but...

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.440
But what?!

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:28.090
I was never counting on the
 Guardian State to begin with.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:31.710
Destroying Tokyo is the only
 way to save the world.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:33.630
Kotetsu. Give me Kurokami Marie's blood crystal.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.470
Huh? Okay.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.170
Where are you going?

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.760
To continue Inuki's research.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.800
This is the only way to save the world.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:46.930
Tsubasa, let's go.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:50.050
I have my own way of doing things.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:51.600
Wait—

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.130
Wait, Kakihara-san!

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:56.770
Do you not understand your noble calling?

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.040
Unless we destroy Tokyo, the
Heroic Lineage will be annihilated!

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:02.310
Is that what you want?!

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:05.280
This was Kurokami's parting gift.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.500
Let's revert the changes.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.040
Midtown Municipal Park | Details
Toyoshima Amusement Park | Details
Mejiro Kusahira Nursery School | Details
Shinagawa Yatsuyama Bridge | Details
Chuo Yodobashi Wholesale Market | Details

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:12.990
This is the AVAL Science Foundation's...

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:17.750
It's the land they've been forcibly acquiring.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:22.420
Kurokami must have discovered something 
and was killed at one of these locations.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.010
I'll avenge her alone.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.100
This is where we part ways.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.840
Do what you want.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.270
Don't say you'll do it alone.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.560
I'm your partner.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.870
We'll start by compiling
 a registry of the list.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:43.520
Yes, sir!

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:58.670
What do you think you're
 doing, Kamina Chihiro?

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:01.670
Have you come to kill me?

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:05.050
No. I just...

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.550
I bet you dreamed of my death.

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.700
Is that true?

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:14.770
What an honor.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:18.820
I can finally cover one of 
the deaths you cause.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:20.620
This is no laughing matter!

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:22.130
Kakihara-san...

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:24.320
Your prophetic dreams seem unavoidable.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:27.870
I couldn't write an article unless
 you let me know beforehand.

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.240
I don't want you to die.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.630
You're going to make me cry.

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.250
Tell me how you really feel.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:37.250
You're not doing it for me.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.750
You're doing it for yourself and Shiraki Yuri.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:44.460
You can't change fate unless you can 
change your prophetic dreams.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:49.090
And you can't change your
 destiny to kill one another, either.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:53.010
I won't deny that.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:54.910
You're awful.

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:57.110
I'm delighted to hear that.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:59.770
Now tell me about how you killed your father.

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:02.780
I don't care if you hate me.

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:05.410
I don't like you, either.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.740
But I have to do something.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:10.730
Nothing will remain.

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:13.760
We will change our destiny.

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:19.160
For Inuki-san and Kurokami-san, 
who trusted us to carry on their mission!

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:22.880
Kakihara-san!

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:27.770
If you don't want me to die, stay away from me.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:30.340
I'll protect Kakihara-san!

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:37.650
Those weren't the eyes of the Kamina 
Chihiro I've been pursuing.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.600
He's trying to live.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:48.280
The plan is coming along smoothly,
 but it's likely we've been discovered.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.860
Tighten your guard.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:53.690
Lay out a trap and kill them.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.780
Let me kill Kamina Chihiro.

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:59.540
No. What can you do with eyes clouded by hate?

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:05.270
Wait, Jun-san!

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.440
Fool.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:13.950
But it's true that Kamina
 Chihiro is an eyesore.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:19.010
He did tempt your daughter, after all.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:22.640
Though we were able to stop it,

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:27.020
the church and the Guardian State nearly
 forming an alliance was a thorn in our sides.

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:30.560
And at the center of it all was Kamina Chihiro.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.150
It was only temporary, but
 he united the Heroic Lineage.

00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:37.880
He may have what it takes to
 become the Lord of Vermilion.

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:47.240
Chihiro-kun...

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.710
Kakihara's next?

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:56.210
Yeah. Chihiro-san said he dreamed it.

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:58.720
And he's trying to stop it alone?

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:00.600
What should we do?

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.550
Are you asking me as a member 
of the Guardian State?

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:06.130
Or as Manazuru Tsubaki?

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:06.850
Huh?

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:11.110
I don't mind helping out a friend.

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:15.240
What did Kurokami find?

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:19.740
The message she left Manazuru
 Tsubaki was her last communication.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:22.330
Her call history...

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:25.210
Her history?

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:35.630
Come to think of it, you never get mad.

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:38.890
Are you in there, Tsubasa?

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:43.600
Is this...

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:50.530
A coincidence?

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:57.010
No. Shoko had us break
 the barriers to destroy Tokyo.

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:01.140
The barriers, huh?

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:07.110
You never give up.

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:11.020
What did you want to discuss?

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:13.840
Don't make me laugh.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.470
You're the one following me.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.930
I just want to protect you.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.810
Well, either way, I was supposed to die.

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:24.590
I wouldn't regret dying at this point.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:30.190
I survived a family suicide, too.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:33.940
Forced into it by debt.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:39.990
In the end, I was abandoned.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:42.300
I was a precocious brat.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:45.450
I knew my parents didn't like me,

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.960
but I still don't know why they left me.

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:59.220
Why did you refuse to die with him?

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.710
Your father wanted to take you with him.

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:04.820
Why did you reject his feelings?

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:12.790
Were you so reluctant to die that
 you were willing to kill your father?

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:15.260
You killed him, didn't you?

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:17.690
You killed your own father so you could live!

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:19.610
I don't care about living!

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:20.960
What?

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:24.630
I don't remember what happened that day.

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:27.280
But I've suffered ever since then!

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:30.180
When I think that I may 
have killed my father,

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:35.630
I really wish I would've died instead!

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:39.630
But there must be some reason I survived!

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:46.970
So I can't die yet.

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:50.300
Those are the eyes.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:51.890
Why?

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:58.530
Your eyes were always dark,
 no matter how cheerful you acted.

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:00.650
Regret and despair.

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:04.860
I sensed that you sought forgiveness

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:08.290
even though you killed your own father.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:10.430
I couldn't forgive you.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:15.000
If you were going to despair,
 why didn't you die with your father?

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:18.300
You wanna live? Then don't walk around
 looking like you've got no hope left!

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:22.800
I don't care who forgives you. I never will!

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:29.340
Or so I thought.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:33.780
But you have the eyes of a man trying to live.

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:38.180
Even after being betrayed by a woman,
 being abandoned by your friends,

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:41.450
and losing everything.

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:47.360
Did you really kill your father?

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:51.170
What are we doing here?

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:55.830
There were GPS coordinates
 on Kurokami's call history.

00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:58.280
Did you call anyone?

00:12:58.850 --> 00:12:59.950
Kotetsu.

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:05.040
Kakihara-san, why did you talk to me last night?

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:07.720
Because I wanted to know the truth.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.680
Kakihara, you're a journalist.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.680
Can you see the truth
 through those warped eyes?

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:17.150
I don't know why I told you that.

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:21.490
I don't know why I'm here walking with you.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:27.240
But if I leave things there,
 then I'm no journalist at all.

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:31.520
You think there's a reason you survived, huh?

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:32.320
Yes.

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:41.170
This device probably
 creates artificial barriers.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:42.580
Barriers?

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:46.120
Based on the data Kurokami left,

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:49.420
seven similar devices likely 
exist around the city.

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:51.750
What does this mean?

00:13:52.110 --> 00:13:56.690
They're trying to build
 new barriers themselves.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:14:01.190
There's no point in Shoko trying
 so hard to destroy the old ones.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:03.690
Is that what the machine is for?

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:06.930
This is for something else.

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:09.360
For their next big plan.

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:11.800
The Second Great Collapse.

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:13.620
Correct.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:19.390
But, poor Icarus, you've
 flown too close to the sun.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.170
Look out!

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:25.550
Kakihara-san, I will protect you!

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:30.870
Kark Kaburagi?

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:32.440
You know him?

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:35.460
You don't? He's a famous pianist.

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:37.270
Even I've got his CD's.

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:41.690
The world calls me a decadent musician.

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:47.280
Now, listen and die to the beautiful
 requiem I offer up to you.

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:50.700
No, you don't!

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:55.350
Tsubasa!

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:56.980
How'd she hit her from there?

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:59.000
You're the one who killed Kurokami.

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:04.700
The reaper doesn't remember
 all those he's granted death.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:06.760
Bastard...

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:12.470
Death comes for all.

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:18.140
Dad?

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:28.030
What's wrong?

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:30.950
No...

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:33.910
Don't, Dad.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.160
Pull yourself together, Kamina!

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:45.420
What do you think of the title "Binding Spell?"

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.770
Break his spell!

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:50.170
That should be easy with your power!

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:53.660
I can't manifest my blood armaments!

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:54.640
What?

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:57.760
My melodies capture people's hearts.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:00.430
You must be very guilty.

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:03.270
Your heart refuses to break free.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:05.670
Kakihara-san?

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:07.730
Why am I doing this?

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:11.240
The unwelcome disrupt my beautiful melodies.

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:14.470
Run! Quickly!

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:17.830
I still have questions for you.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:20.000
You're not escaping to the afterlife!

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:22.250
Then you will die together.

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:23.920
Kakihara-san!

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:28.650
Tsubasa!

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:34.360
Kakihara-san.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:42.530
<i>Live.</i>

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.400
Live.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:51.050
Tsubasa!

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:57.320
No need to grieve. Death is
 but a moment's parting.

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:01.000
Kakihara-san?

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:06.670
I hear the wailing of your soul.

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:08.400
Shut up!

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:12.310
You're one more note.

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:15.930
Play for me the rhapsody of death.

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:20.390
Kakihara-san!

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:29.090
Cerdid!

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:32.290
You'll pay for hurting Chihiro!

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:36.480
Why did you save me?

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:43.160
Making you admit your guilt 
was my life's purpose.

00:17:44.060 --> 00:17:47.470
I didn't want to acknowledge
 that my parents rejected me.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.980
If you love someone,
 you should take them with you.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:55.680
So I couldn't forgive you for
 refusing to die with him.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:00.280
But it seems I was wrong.

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:01.820
I lost sight of the tru—

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:02.640
Kakihara-san!

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:04.640
Chihiro, run!

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:08.900
You didn't kill your father.

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:12.900
I reviewed the case documents again.

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:18.530
He must have returned to his
senses when he was stabbed.

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:25.080
He feared his own actions
 and knew he had to save you.

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:29.450
So you wouldn't be a murderer.

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:33.500
So you'd live.

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:35.300
<b>Live</b>

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:39.300
I didn't kill my father...

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.840
You didn't kill him!

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:44.930
Kark!

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:53.460
Kakihara-san!

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:56.820
Are you okay, Chihiro-san?!

00:18:56.820 --> 00:19:00.200
Kotetsu, that's the man who killed Kurokami-san!

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:02.470
That bastard killed Marie?

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:04.460
Let's go, Kotecchan!

00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:05.200
Yeah.

00:19:05.480 --> 00:19:07.330
That's all for today.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:10.170
Hey, wait!

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:14.170
Cerdid...

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:18.930
No...

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:20.870
Don't you feel relieved?

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:27.250
It's not like me to die protecting you.

00:19:31.010 --> 00:19:33.260
Maybe I was jealous.

00:19:33.410 --> 00:19:33.940
What?

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:37.010
Nothing. It's in the past now.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:41.950
In the end, you and I were the same.

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:45.630
Sorry.

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:48.730
It's fine.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:50.840
Live.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:54.560
Live, Kamina Chihiro.

00:19:55.110 --> 00:20:00.210
Kurokami, Akaya Inuki, Tsubasa,

00:20:00.810 --> 00:20:04.800
your father, and I have a message for you.

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:08.700
You have to live. Live.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:10.660
Kakihara-san...

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:13.330
There's a reason you survived.

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:20.500
Maybe I was left alive
 so I could tell you this.

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:26.140
Someday, you'll tell someone...

00:20:27.230 --> 00:20:29.310
Kakihara-san. Kakihara-san...

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:30.650
Tsubasa...

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:37.710
Dad, Mom...

00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:39.540
Kakihara-san!

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:50.190
Another.

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:53.410
Fate is truly unfaithful.

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:57.850
When Kotetsu was spared,
I thought it was a rare blessing.

00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:00.000
So why, why?

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.940
However, at this rate...

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:05.910
Yes. They'll be annihilated again.

00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:07.650
Again?

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:13.410
Even if Tokyo is destroyed,
 Chaos' plan may not be stopped.

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:17.780
If the last one is connected, there
 will be a Second Great Collapse.

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:20.700
Chaos wins.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:23.260
I will not let that happen.

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:26.430
The time has come to settle this.

00:21:27.130 --> 00:21:32.430
We cannot retreat until we're down
to the last of the Heroic Lineage.

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:35.150
Yes, absolutely.

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:39.160
For the splendid new world.
